Subject: [PATCH 06/12] LvglLib: Move the cursor with relative pointers

The pointer input device reads EFI_ABSOLUTE_POINTER_PROTOCOL only: USB
mice through UsbMouseAbsolutePointerDxe, and touch screens. The
TrackPoint and the touchpad of a laptop are PS/2 mice, which
Ps2MouseDxe exposes as EFI_SIMPLE_POINTER_PROTOCOL, so they do not move
the cursor.

Read the simple pointer of the console (the ConSplitter, which merges
all of them) too, once per frame like the absolute one. Its motion, in
counts at the resolution of the protocol, moves the cursor 8 pixels per
mm, twice as fast for the part of a read beyond 6 pixels; the fraction
of a pixel is kept for the next read. The left button clicks. The
cursor still appears only once a pointer moves or clicks.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
